---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const LAST_UPDATED = '25 April 2026';
const COMPANY_NAME = 'Servogo';
const COMPANY_LEGAL = 'Tobsoft Ltd';
const COMPANY_NUMBER = '17180232';
const COMPANY_EMAIL = 'support@servogo.co.uk';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service | Servogo"
  description="Terms of Service for Servogo, the field service management platform operated by Tobsoft Ltd."
>

<div class="legal-shell">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
          <a href="/">Home</a>
          <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
          <span>Terms of Service</span>
        </nav>

        <h1 style="font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.025em; margin: 0 0 8px; color: var(--ink);">Terms of Service</h1>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-tertiary); margin: 0 0 48px;">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

        <div class="prose legal-prose">
          <p class="legal-intro">
            These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of the {COMPANY_NAME} platform
            ("Service") operated by {COMPANY_LEGAL} (trading as {COMPANY_NAME}) ("we", "us", "our").
            By creating an account or using the Service you agree to these Terms. If you are agreeing
            on behalf of a business you represent that you have authority to bind that business.
          </p>

          <h2>1. The Service</h2>
          <p>{COMPANY_NAME} is a field service management platform that helps businesses schedule
          technicians, manage client routes, generate invoices, and track service visits. We
          grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to access and use the
          Service for your internal business operations during your subscription period.</p>

          <h2>2. Accounts</h2>
          <h3>2.1 Eligibility</h3>
          <p>You must be at least 18 years old and have the legal capacity to enter into a
          binding contract. The Service is intended for businesses, not individual consumers.</p>
          <h3>2.2 Account security</h3>
          <p>You are responsible for keeping your login credentials confidential and for all
          activity that occurs under your account. Notify us immediately at {COMPANY_EMAIL} if
          you suspect unauthorised access.</p>
          <h3>2.3 Accurate information</h3>
          <p>You must provide accurate, current, and complete information when creating your
          account and keep it up to date.</p>

          <h2>3. Subscriptions and Billing</h2>
          <h3>3.1 Plans and fees</h3>
          <p>Subscriptions are billed in advance on a monthly or annual basis. Current pricing
          is displayed on our <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a> and may change with 30 days' notice.</p>
          <h3>3.2 Payment</h3>
          <p>Payments are processed by Stripe, Inc. By providing payment details you authorise
          us to charge the applicable fees. All fees are exclusive of VAT unless stated
          otherwise; applicable VAT will be added at checkout.</p>
          <h3>3.3 Seat-based billing</h3>
          <p>Team and Pro plans are priced per active team member. Adding members to your
          organisation will adjust your subscription quantity at the next billing cycle.</p>
          <h3>3.4 Free trial</h3>
          <p>Where we offer a free trial period, no charge is made until the trial ends. You
          may cancel before the trial ends to avoid being charged.</p>
          <h3>3.5 Refunds</h3>
          <p>We offer a 30-day money-back guarantee on your first subscription payment. After
          that, fees are non-refundable except where required by law. If we materially reduce
          the functionality of the Service we will offer a pro-rata refund for the unused
          period.</p>
          <h3>3.6 Failed payments</h3>
          <p>If a payment fails your account will enter a grace period. Continued failure will
          result in your account being restricted to read-only access until payment is resolved.</p>

          <h2>4. Acceptable Use</h2>
          <p>You may not use the Service to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Violate any applicable law or regulation.</li>
            <li>Upload, store, or transmit unlawful, harmful, or fraudulent content.</li>
            <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to any part of the Service or its infrastructure.</li>
            <li>Reverse-engineer, decompile, or otherwise attempt to extract the source code of the Service.</li>
            <li>Resell or sub-licence access to the Service without our written consent.</li>
            <li>Use the Service in a way that places unreasonable load on our infrastructure.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We reserve the right to suspend or terminate access for any violation of this section.</p>

          <h2>5. Your Data</h2>
          <h3>5.1 Ownership</h3>
          <p>You retain all rights to the data you upload or create in the Service ("Customer
          Data"). We do not claim ownership of your Customer Data.</p>
          <h3>5.2 Licence to us</h3>
          <p>You grant us a limited licence to store, process, and transmit Customer Data solely
          as necessary to provide and improve the Service.</p>
          <h3>5.3 Data processing</h3>
          <p>Where we process personal data on your behalf (e.g. employee or client records) we
          act as a data processor and you act as the data controller. Our Privacy Policy and
          the data processing terms incorporated therein apply. You are responsible for having a
          lawful basis to input personal data into the Service and for obtaining any necessary
          consents from your clients and staff.</p>
          <h3>5.4 Data export</h3>
          <p>You may export your Customer Data at any time via the Service's export features or
          the API. On termination of your account we will make your data available for export
          for 30 days, after which it may be deleted in accordance with our retention policy.</p>

          <h2>6. Intellectual Property</h2>
          <p>The Service, including its software, design, and content (excluding Customer Data),
          is owned by {COMPANY_NAME} and protected by copyright, trademark, and other
          intellectual property laws. These Terms do not grant you any rights in the Service
          other than the limited licence described in Section 1.</p>

          <h2>7. Confidentiality</h2>
          <p>Each party agrees to keep the other's non-public information confidential and not
          to disclose it to third parties without consent, except as required by law or to
          deliver the Service. This obligation survives termination of these Terms for three
          years.</p>

          <h2>8. Warranties and Disclaimers</h2>
          <p>We provide the Service on an "as is" and "as available" basis. To the fullest
          extent permitted by law we disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including
          merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. We do not
          warrant that the Service will be error-free, uninterrupted, or meet your specific
          requirements.</p>

          <h2>9. Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, {COMPANY_NAME}'s aggregate
          liability to you for any claims arising out of or relating to these Terms or the
          Service is limited to the fees you paid in the 12 months preceding the claim.</p>
          <p>Neither party is liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or
          punitive damages, or loss of profits, revenue, data, or goodwill, even if advised
          of the possibility of such damages.</p>
          <p>Nothing in these Terms limits liability for fraud, death or personal injury caused
          by negligence, or any liability that cannot be excluded by law.</p>

          <h2>10. Indemnification</h2>
          <p>You agree to indemnify and hold harmless {COMPANY_NAME} and its officers,
          directors, employees, and agents from any claims, losses, or expenses (including
          reasonable legal fees) arising from your use of the Service, your Customer Data, or
          your violation of these Terms.</p>

          <h2>11. Termination</h2>
          <h3>11.1 By you</h3>
          <p>You may cancel your subscription at any time through the billing portal. Cancellation
          takes effect at the end of the current billing period. No partial-period refunds are
          given unless covered by Section 3.5.</p>
          <h3>11.2 By us</h3>
          <p>We may suspend or terminate your account immediately if you breach these Terms, fail
          to pay fees after a grace period, or if we are required to do so by law. We may also
          discontinue the Service with 60 days' notice.</p>
          <h3>11.3 Effect of termination</h3>
          <p>On termination, your right to access the Service ceases. Sections 5, 6, 7, 9, 10,
          13, and 14 survive termination.</p>

          <h2>12. Changes to the Terms</h2>
          <p>We may update these Terms from time to time. We will notify you of material changes
          by email or by a prominent notice in the Service at least 14 days before they take
          effect. Continued use of the Service after the effective date constitutes acceptance
          of the updated Terms.</p>

          <h2>13. Governing Law and Disputes</h2>
          <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales. Any disputes shall be
          subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of England and Wales, except
          where mandatory consumer protection law in your country provides otherwise.</p>

          <h2>14. General</h2>
          <p>These Terms, together with the Privacy Policy and any order forms, constitute the
          entire agreement between you and {COMPANY_NAME} regarding the Service and supersede
          all prior agreements. If any provision is found unenforceable it will be modified to
          the minimum extent necessary; remaining provisions continue in full force. Our failure
          to enforce any right is not a waiver of that right. You may not assign these Terms
          without our written consent; we may assign them without restriction.</p>

          <h2>15. Contact</h2>
          <p>Questions about these Terms? Contact us at <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY_EMAIL}`}>{COMPANY_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 32px; border-top: 1px solid var(--stroke-regular); display: flex; gap: 16px;">
          <a href="/privacy" class="btn btn-secondary">Privacy Policy</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

</Base>
